/-
Johnson/G/XShapeLit.lean: the shape part of what the reader of the program `verify-on-bytes` makes
of the public files, at the full size, written out whole: the value of the projection `xShapeOf`
(Johnson/Desc/Ok/PlanWritten/XShape.lean). Data alone: one definition.

What stands where.
  First the 25 segments, 0 to 24, each as: some (the number of the committed matrices of its
    approximate range proof, for each matrix (label, rows, columns), the list that names each
    matrix's symbol array). 176 matrices in all.
  Then the seven parts of the head's plan: nU; ns; funClosed; lidb; the call z1.call; the call
    z2.call; and the eleven places of f9: its calls, dT, kT, NT, rK, NC, cK, iota, first, callOf,
    pub.
  A call's ten places: name, n, iota, k, kappa, fn, t0, tau, pub, heavy. At all four calls tau is
    none: no public table stands here.

Whence. Made by program from a print of `xShapeOf Z.p.X` at the public part Z of the IOP as written
in Lean at the stored full-size public files: Lean's evaluator, the library's own printer, 5569
bytes, parsed whole. That the program wrote what the print says is held by
parsing this file's definition and comparing it with the parsed print, value by value, by program.
By the printer's own run the value's hash is one at six sets of public files, with other free
numbers and other scales. A second evaluation, by the library's own reader at every build, is
Johnson/G/XShapeLitGuard.lean; its head says how far the two evaluations are apart. No
theorem says that a reader returns this value.


-/
